<section>
  <div class="wrap two two--top">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--blue">The Cambridge core</p>
      <h2>Three subjects, all of them in English</h2>
      <p>Three lessons every morning, one of each, each with a teacher who has a degree in the subject. Then History or Executive Function until lunch.</p>
      <p>We are an English language center, and at this age the Cambridge subjects are how we teach the language. A thirteen-year-old will not sit through vocabulary drills. They will argue about whose experiment was fair, and that argument has to happen in English.</p>
      <h3>Maths</h3>
      <p>Less counting, more reasoning, and a lot of showing your working. Half of a word problem is reading it properly, and every answer gets explained out loud: what you did, why it works, where the other method went wrong.</p>
      <h3>Science</h3>
      <p>Biology, chemistry and physics, with practical work every week: a ramp on the classroom floor, plants along the window, a bench full of samples. The English is in the write-up — method, results, what the numbers actually say — and in defending it.</p>
      <h3>English</h3>
      <p>The lesson where the language itself is the subject. Whole books, literature and argument: a position to take, evidence for it, and the writing to make it stand up.</p>
      <p>A student who can explain a fair test has learned some science and a lot of English. That is the whole idea: the subject gives them something worth saying, and the language to say it.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="leaf-wrap leaf-wrap--r has-sticker">
        <span class="sticker sticker--blue sticker--tr">Cambridge Lower Secondary</span>
        {% photo "secondary-ramp-experiment", "photo--lg photo--tilt-r" %}
      </div>
      {% set collageWide = false %}{% set collageArt = false %}{% set collage2up = false %}{% set collageCredit = "" %}
